WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.360
This mom cuts the head and the tail off a fish before cooking it.

2
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:07.360
What a waste.

3
00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:08.820
Her daughter asks,

4
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.020
Why do you do this?

5
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.340
The mom says,

6
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:12.660
Because my mom did it that way.

7
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:17.360
So the daughter calls Grandma and asks the same question.

8
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.300
Grandma, why?

9
00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:19.620
Grandma says,

10
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.700
Because my mom did it that way.

11
00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:27.180
So the daughter visits Great Grandma and asks the same question.

12
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.580
Why do we cut the head and the tail of the fish?

13
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.440
The Great Grandma laughs and says,

14
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:39.260
Oh, I only cut it because in 1950, my pan was too small.

15
00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:40.100
That's it.

16
00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.900
It was not a recipe, not a tradition.

17
00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.280
Great Grandma just had a tiny pan and we never questioned it.

18
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.340
We do this in life, in religion, in culture, in government.

19
00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.660
We follow tradition and we don't know why.

20
00:00:55.660 --> 00:01:01.660
So maybe it's time to ask why a little bit more often.

21
00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:10.500
If you throw a frog into boiling water, it jumps out immediately.

22
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.560
It knows it's in danger and it saves its life.

23
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.140
What the heck, bro?

24
00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:18.000
Did you just try to kill me?

25
00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:23.440
But if you put it in warm water and slowly turn up the heat,

26
00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.240
Oh, spa day!

27
00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:27.940
And a bit more heat,

28
00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:30.460
Okay, who turned the sauna on?

29
00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.900
And a bit more heat,

30
00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.480
This is trying to kill me!

31
00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:38.940
The frog dies.

32
00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:39.680
The frog dies.

33
00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:42.880
Not because it couldn't jump,

34
00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:46.900
But because it didn't notice in time.

35
00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.160
Let this be a lesson in life.

36
00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:54.360
Sometimes, danger doesn't hit you all at once.

37
00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.980
It creeps in, slowly but surely.

38
00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:03.400
A toxic relationship, a bad job, a terrible living condition.

39
00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:06.400
Slowly then, you're dead.

40
00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:09.360
So ask yourself,

41
00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:12.160
What pot are you sitting in?

42
00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:14.860
And is it time to jump?
